The dataset was examined for missing values before model development. No missing values were detected; therefore, no imputation or deletion procedures were required. Consequently, all observations were retained throughout the analysis.

### Leakage Prevention

Several safeguards were implemented to prevent information leakage from the holdout test set. First, the train-test split was performed before any preprocessing. Second, scaling parameters were estimated exclusively from the training data. Third, five-fold cross-validation and model tuning were conducted only on the training observations. Finally, the holdout test set remained untouched until the final model evaluation. These procedures ensure that performance estimates reflect the models' ability to generalize to unseen data.

