The stepwise AIC procedure retained all predictors in the initial OLS model, as the full specification achieved the lowest AIC score of -47.29. Although variables like lweight, lcp, and pgg45 have p-values above 0.05, AIC evaluates the overall balance of model fit and complexity rather than individual significance. As shown in the deletion analysis, omitting any predictor inflates the AIC metric—for instance, excluding lcp or lweight increases the AIC to -47.08 and -45.98, respectively. Consequently, removing any variable fails to improve the model, justifying the retention of the full linear specification as the baseline for subsequent Ridge and Lasso comparisons.


