The two tuning rules address different decision objectives. The **\(\lambda_{min}\)** rule selects the value of the regularization parameter that minimizes the estimated cross-validation error, making it the preferred choice when maximizing predictive accuracy is the primary objective. In contrast, the **\(\lambda_{1SE}\)** rule chooses the largest value of \(\lambda\) whose cross-validation error remains within one standard error of the minimum. This criterion intentionally favors stronger regularization to obtain a simpler and potentially more stable model while accepting only a small reduction in predictive accuracy.

