Overall, predictive performance and interpretability represent different model-selection criteria. Models selected by **\(\lambda_{min}\)** prioritize minimizing prediction error, whereas models selected by **\(\lambda_{1SE}\)** prioritize simplicity and robustness. Given the small difference in cross-validation performance but the substantial improvement in model sparsity, **Lasso with \(\lambda_{1SE}\)** is selected as the preferred model before evaluating performance on the holdout test set.

